-- title:
--   Rigidity of mathcal O_{2,n}-points in a local algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime and let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi$ an irreducible element, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, with $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, $Fr$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $Onr$, with $Onr$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, $(\pi)$ maximal in $Onr$, every element of $Onr$ a root modulo $\pi$ of some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr\,x \equiv x^{r} \bmod \pi$ for all $x$. Write $\mathcal O_2$ for the equaliser subalgebra $\{x : Fr(Fr\,x) = x\} \subseteq Onr$ and, for $n : \mathbb N$, $\mathcal O_{2,n} = \mathcal O_2/(\pi^{n+1})$. Let $Fr_2$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $\mathcal O_{2,n}$ such that $Fr_2$ sends the class of $y \in \mathcal O_2$ to the class of any $y' \in \mathcal O_2$ with $y' = Fr\,y$ in $Onr$. Then for every local commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ and any two $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\varepsilon, \varepsilon' : \mathcal O_{2,n} \to B$, either $\varepsilon' = \varepsilon$ or $\varepsilon' = \varepsilon \circ Fr_2$.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement for $\mathcal O_{2,n}$-valued points used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: the group generated by $Fr_2$ acts simply on the set of $\mathcal O$-algebra maps from $\mathcal O_{2,n}$ into a local algebra. It is applied to the geometric and adic fibres of the descended quotient map, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_fib`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_fib) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_adicFib`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_adicFib).
